  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="5d64227b-be1e-5578-ad36-814002798047" activityNameId="4364732d-a502-5cff-a259-fae3b2ede85a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heavy fuel oil, burned in refinery furnace</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heavy fuel oil, burned in refinery furnace
Description of the direct emissions due to the combustion of fuel in refinery furnaces and generators not including the infrastructure of the furnace.;
Synonyms: Schweröl, HFO; 
UUID: bcbd8e8c-ced7-3edc-a277-7b275bbcc78c
Consumption of heavy fuel oil and combustion emissions.
Location: Data for single European plants.
Technology: Average technology in use. There might be large differences for single plants due to the technology used for the flue gas treatment.
Time period: European data for regulated emissions CO2, NOx, SOx, Ni and V have been provided by some refineries. They have been compared and discussed with older literature data. Literature data have been used for other emissions.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Environmental reports, public statistics and literature data. 
Extrapolations: From single plants to average situation.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_bcbd8e8c-ced7-3edc-a277-7b275bbcc78c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">RER</shortname>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Location: Data for single European plants.</text>
        </comment>
      </geography>
      <technology>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Technology: Average technology in use. There might be large differences for single plants due to the technology used for the flue gas treatment.</text>
        </comment>
      </technology>
      <timePeriod startDate="1980-01-01" endDate="2000-12-31" isDataValidForEntirePeriod="true">
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Time period: European data for regulated emissions CO2, NOx, SOx, Ni and V have been provided by some refineries. They have been compared and discussed with older literature data. Literature data have been used for other emissions.</text>
        </comment>
      </timePeriod>
